/-!
# Christoffel variation tables of the fundamental Birmingham–Mokhtari scalar jet

Closed forms of the linearized Christoffel variation `Linearization.connection J K u i j`, the
quadratic Christoffel variation `Quadratic.connection J K u i j` and its spatial derivative
`Quadratic.connectionSpatial J K k u i j` for the fundamental scalar metric jet `K` over the
Birmingham–Mokhtari background `J`, in every index order. Each entry is a rational function of
`(s, r)` times a monomial in the angular jet times a power of `y`; vanishing entries are recorded as
such. The proofs use the index-collapsed forms over a diagonal background, the entry tables of the
two jets, and one power-cancellation pass, all at the default heartbeat limit. These tables make the
scalar–scalar quadratic Ricci variation an assembly of compact pieces.
-/

